stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  accTitle: x402 payment lifecycle (V2, all three payment flows)
  accDescr: State diagram: x402 payment lifecycle (V2, all three payment flows). 11 states: Unpaid request, Payment required (402), Payload received, Verified, Committed before execution, Handler executed, Settlement pending, Settled, Rejected, Responded 200, and Voided or reclaimed. Starts in Unpaid request. Ends in Rejected, Responded 200, and Voided or reclaimed. 18 transitions. From Unpaid request to Payment required (402) when Server sends 402 (HTTP 402 + PAYMENT-REQUIRED). From Payment required (402) to Payload received when Client retries with a signed payload (PAYMENT-SIGNATURE header). From Payload received to Rejected when Malformed payload or unsupported scheme, network or flow (HTTP 400). From Payload received to Verified when authorization flow: facilitator returns isValid true (POST /verify). From Payload received to Rejected when Facilitator returns isValid false (POST /verify, then HTTP 402). From Payload received to Rejected when Facilitator unreachable (@x402/express answers 502 SDK behavior, not in the spec) (HTTP 502). From Payload received to Committed before execution when upfront or escrow flow: first settle succeeds (POST /settle). From Verified to Handler executed when Handler runs. From Committed before execution to Handler executed when Handler runs. From Handler executed to Settled when authorization flow: settle succeeds, or escrow: capture succeeds (POST /settle). From Handler executed to Settlement pending when Settle broadcast but not confirmed, or timed out (POST /settle). From Settlement pending to Settled when Server reconciles on chain and finds the transfer. From Settlement pending to Rejected when Reconciliation shows no transfer and one retry fails (POST /settle). From Handler executed to Rejected when Settle fails (for example insufficient_funds) (HTTP 402 + PAYMENT-RESPONSE success false). From Handler executed to Voided or reclaimed when escrow: server voids the hold (POST /settle with payload.type void). From Handler executed to Voided or reclaimed when escrow: client reclaims an untouched hold after captureDeadline (reclaim called by the client on the escrow contract (never relayed through the facilitator)). From Settled to Responded 200 when Server returns the resource (HTTP 200 + PAYMENT-RESPONSE). From Handler executed to Responded 200 when upfront: payment already settled, server returns the resource (HTTP 200 + PAYMENT-RESPONSE).
  state "Unpaid request" as s_unpaid
  state "Payment required (402)" as s_payment_required
  state "Payload received" as s_payload_received
  state "Verified" as s_verified
  state "Committed before execution" as s_held
  state "Handler executed" as s_executed
  state "Settlement pending" as s_settle_pending
  state "Settled" as s_settled
  state "Rejected" as s_rejected
  state "Responded 200" as s_responded
  state "Voided or reclaimed" as s_voided
  [*] --> s_unpaid
  s_unpaid --> s_payment_required : Server sends 402
  s_payment_required --> s_payload_received : Client retries with a signed payload
  s_payload_received --> s_rejected : Malformed payload or unsupported scheme, network or flow
  s_payload_received --> s_verified : authorization flow: facilitator returns isValid true
  s_payload_received --> s_rejected : Facilitator returns isValid false
  s_payload_received --> s_rejected : Facilitator unreachable (@x402/express answers 502, SDK behavior, not in the spec)
  s_payload_received --> s_held : upfront or escrow flow: first settle succeeds
  s_verified --> s_executed : Handler runs
  s_held --> s_executed : Handler runs
  s_executed --> s_settled : authorization flow: settle succeeds, or escrow: capture succeeds
  s_executed --> s_settle_pending : Settle broadcast but not confirmed, or timed out
  s_settle_pending --> s_settled : Server reconciles on chain and finds the transfer
  s_settle_pending --> s_rejected : Reconciliation shows no transfer and one retry fails
  s_executed --> s_rejected : Settle fails (for example insufficient_funds)
  s_executed --> s_voided : escrow: server voids the hold
  s_executed --> s_voided : escrow: client reclaims an untouched hold after captureDeadline
  s_settled --> s_responded : Server returns the resource
  s_executed --> s_responded : upfront: payment already settled, server returns the resource
  s_rejected --> [*]
  s_responded --> [*]
  s_voided --> [*]
  note right of s_unpaid : No PAYMENT-SIGNATURE header.
  note right of s_payment_required : PAYMENT-REQUIRED header sent with the accepts list.
  note right of s_payload_received : PAYMENT-SIGNATURE decoded#59; the flow comes from extra.paymentFlow.
  note right of s_verified : authorization flow only. /verify is read-only.
  note right of s_held : upfront#58; settled. escrow#58; deposit or hold placed.
  note right of s_settle_pending : errorReason settlement_pending#59; transaction hash present.
  note right of s_settled : success true#59; PAYMENT-RESPONSE carries the transaction hash.
  note right of s_rejected : 400 for a malformed payload and 402 for a failed payment (spec)#59; the @x402/express middleware answers 502 when the facilitator is unreachable (SDK behavior).
  note right of s_voided : auth-capture escrow only.
